@startuml ai_provider_recommendation
' --------------------------------------------------------------
' AI Provider Recommendation Architecture (Fig 3.10)
' Shows how an AI chat session yields a ranked list of verified providers.
' --------------------------------------------------------------
title Clinix - AI Provider Recommendation Architecture

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Inter, Helvetica, sans-serif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #EAF2F9
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F5F9FC
skinparam ActorBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam ArrowColor #555555

actor "Patient" as Patient

rectangle "Mobile App (Flutter)" #F0F7FB {
  component "AI Symptom Checker\nScreen" as UI
}

rectangle "Clinix Backend (Django)" #F0F7FB {
  component "AI Consultation\nSession Manager"             as Session
  component "Google Gemini\nClient"                        as Gemini
  component "Structured Assessment\nGenerator"             as Assess
  component "Provider Recommender\n(scoring service)"      as Reco
  database  "Verified Providers\n(approved only)"          as Providers
  database  "Vitals\n(heart rate, HRV,\nactivity)"          as Vitals
}

cloud "Google Gemini API\n(pre-trained, external)" as GeminiAPI #FFF7E0

Patient --> UI               : 1. Symptoms +/- image
UI      --> Session          : 2. POST /ai/chat/<id>/message
Session --> Vitals           : 3. Read latest vitals
Vitals  --> Session          : silent context
Session --> Gemini           : 4. prompt + history\n+ vitals (hidden)
Gemini  --> GeminiAPI        : 5. inference
GeminiAPI --> Gemini         : reply
Gemini  --> Session          : next question /\nclarification
Session --> UI               : reply
UI      --> Patient          : conversation turn

... when patient ends session OR asks for a doctor ...

UI      --> Session          : POST /chat/<id>/complete\nor /chat/<id>/recommend
Session --> Assess           : request structured\nassessment
Assess  --> Gemini           : extract { summary,\n  triage_priority,\n  recommended_specialty,\n  possible_causes,\n  red_flags }
Gemini  --> Assess           : JSON assessment
Assess  --> Reco             : recommended_specialty +\npatient location +\nlanguage + budget
Reco    --> Providers        : filter verification_status='approved'\nWHERE specialty matches
Providers --> Reco           : candidate providers
Reco    --> Reco             : score each candidate\n(specialty, rating, distance,\nlanguage, fee, online status)
Reco    --> UI               : top-K providers\n+ match_reasons[]
UI      --> Patient          : "Doctors that match your symptoms"

note right of Reco
  Transparent rules-based scorer.
  No model is trained on patient data.
  Every match is explained by a
  human-readable match_reasons string.
end note

note bottom of Gemini
  Pre-trained external model
  invoked per session. Clinix
  does not perform any model
  training in-house.
end note
@enduml
